      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:7f9afb28e4ff832ce186d53d1743f3b94e0732c1b7f5b64f3bfedd4116078cde\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:9a28ee72e2ba7db2b4bd91151a5725190ec8b657e91a78c1845f8e6bf816d14f\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:6ecafc5e2b442c608b9bdb008bf95a13a20723c9fbcf861785c623d134f302d6\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:9ccf312ac7197143c018c89fbe479551127628aa834b91f60e4be44d3cb52a19\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:fb177adddb4b4eab97d02b7903c30af4cc3b9e644fe9bb5bd113bbbc57651144\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":5933,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5597,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5594:5597:sha256-ee4d988c65de860fabbfbcd27f73d50bbebe3fba37fe419284f4811389c30bdc\",\"quote\":\"may\",\"start\":5594},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:c1d39af2f90536eb8e9f17770199caaf2461bf39f87ce54124a5a7ab746adb75\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"statement\",\"logic_text\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:fb177adddb4b4eab97d02b7903c30af4cc3b9e644fe9bb5bd113bbbc57651144\",\"modality\":\"possible\",\"modality_quote\":\"may\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:00bef07c0745db88def5f2d9985cc2bf0b60524342b0fd263e8e62221432f448\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"references\":[],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:0380b7106c91b6370024d4f71567e06300c93285dce87ff137dd6098863b9cad\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\"],\"scope_text\":\"When an employee is on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":5370,\"summary\":\"An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
      "dcterms:references": [
